{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"036443e5-7cb5-4041-a502-54ef5f0d47dd","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\n  \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\n    \"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\",\n    \"additionalContext\": \"<EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>\\nYou have superpowers.\\n\\n**Below is the full content of your 'superpowers:using-superpowers' skill - your introduction to using skills. For all other skills, use the 'Skill' tool:**\\n\\n---\\nname: using-superpowers\\ndescription: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring skill invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions\\n---\\n\\n<SUBAGENT-STOP>\\nIf you were dispatched as a subagent to execute a specific task, ignore this skill.\\n</SUBAGENT-STOP>\\n\\n<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\\n\\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\\n\\nThis is not negotiable. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\\n\\n## The Rule\\n\\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action** — including clarifying questions, exploring the codebase, or checking files. If it turns out wrong for the situation, you don't have to use it.\\n\\n**Before entering plan mode:** if you haven't already brainstormed, invoke the brainstorming skill first.\\n\\nThen announce \\\"Using [skill] to [purpose]\\\" and follow the skill exactly. If it has a checklist, create a todo per item.\\n\\n## Skill Priority\\n\\nWhen multiple skills apply, process skills come first — they set the approach, then implementation skills (frontend-design, etc.) carry it out. Brainstorming and systematic-debugging are Superpowers' most common process skills, but the rule holds for any of them.\\n\\n- \\\"Let's build X\\\" → superpowers:brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\\n- \\\"Fix this bug\\\" → superpowers:systematic-debugging first, then domain skills.\\n\\n## Red Flags\\n\\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:\\n\\n| Thought | Reality |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| \\\"This is just a simple question\\\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\\n| \\\"I need more context first\\\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\\n| \\\"Let me explore the codebase first\\\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\\n| \\\"I can check git/files quickly\\\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\\n| \\\"Let me gather information first\\\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\\n| \\\"This doesn't need a formal skill\\\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\\n| \\\"I remember this skill\\\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\\n| \\\"This doesn't count as a task\\\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\\n| \\\"The skill is overkill\\\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\\n| \\\"I'll just do this one thing first\\\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\\n| \\\"This feels productive\\\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\\n| \\\"I know what that means\\\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\\n\\n## Platform Adaptation\\n\\nIf your harness appears here, read its reference file for special instructions:\\n\\n- Claude Code: `references/claude-code-tools.md`\\n- Codex: `references/codex-tools.md`\\n- Pi: `references/pi-tools.md`\\n- Antigravity: `references/antigravity-tools.md`\\n- Hermes Agent: `references/hermes-tools.md`\\n- Muse: `references/muse-tools.md`\\n\\n## User Instructions\\n\\nUser instructions (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md, etc, direct requests) take precedence over skills, which in turn override default behavior. Only skip skill workflows or instructions when your human partner has explicitly told you to.\\n</EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>\"\n  }\n}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"\"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/run-hook.cmd\" session-start","durationMs":510},"type":"attachment","uuid":"35c3f944-fc42-4c20-8914-df06be8b9b38","timestamp":"2026-09-28T12:59:29.380Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"35c3f944-fc42-4c20-8914-df06be8b9b38","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"036443e5-7cb5-4041-a502-54ef5f0d47dd","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python/R. macOS primary since 2026-08-05; Windows 11 still active. Tool paths: CLAUDE.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads\\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\\n- **Status report**: #3 by 9/25, biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: NEXT: phone check; host or local? →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\n- **RTP CLA (9/10)**: NEXT: .ris → Zotero; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla\\n- **ATH Tech**: shipped; ITS pending; run 9/29. →Tier A tech-inventory-refresh\\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve. Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD → Parquet `athlete-snapshots/` on Drive; backup 21:00; nudges on Win. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. Wk4 COLO: EPA layer only, full profile? →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/22)**: 011 awaits Eric/staff; Jev pilot on draft PR #2, shadow only. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **Sleep scheduler (9/16)**: R1 merged. NEXT: night/early-kickoff itineraries. →`sleep-scheduler/`\\n- **RI5 #002 (9/21)**: v2 on Drive. NEXT: Eric sends `_v2` only.\\n- **TypeSafe (9/22)**: shadow gate log-only Win, review ~10/6; spring traj failed. NEXT: Eric Y/Ns 22 surgeries (#21). →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: Swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB (`load_snapshot.py`, PK merge since PR #4). Both machines: 2026 thru wk3 + video plays. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Hooks: patch both copies only for shared events; Codex has no prompt-submit event. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries copy nothing alone; sweep nested `~/.claude` repos. →handoff 2026-09-19-backup-divergence-fix.\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Win: `Desktop\\\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture: Mac only →cfb-forecast-capture. Portfolio dashboard →command-centre.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- **OKR gate (scored 9/14)**: AI integration buy-in + data governance (Anthony). Fold into NCAA charter or park?\\n- **No Kitman vs MyLink**: error, never real. Vendor is Myelin (startup AMS), not pursued. Kitman stays; don't resurface (9/24).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n[2026-09-23T01:01:35.997003+00:00] compiler-backlog: 2 log(s) backlogged, compiling newest 2 this run - run compile.py manually to catch up\\n[2026-09-23T01:01:35.997435+00:00] compiler-stale-lock: reclaimed compile lock held 1531min by pid 59036 (compile.py --auto)\\n[2026-09-23 07:53] daily-backup: 1 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n[2026-09-24 09:01] daily-backup: 1 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n[2026-09-25T00:47:13.718670+00:00] compiler-backlog: 3 log(s) backlogged, compiling newest 2 this run - run compile.py manually to catch up\\n[2026-09-24 21:18] daily-backup: 1 error(s): manifest-unmanaged:RunningTheRoom - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n[2026-09-25T02:25:56.465559+00:00] compiler-backlog: 2 log(s) backlogged, compiling newest 2 this run - run compile.py manually to catch up\\n[2026-09-26 11:38] daily-backup: 2 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, manifest-unmanaged:RunningTheRoom - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n[2026-09-26T16:26:03-0500] perch-pull: error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\\n[2026-09-27T00:34:58-0500] perch-pull: error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\\n[2026-09-27 11:05] daily-backup: 2 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, manifest-unmanaged:RunningTheRoom - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n[2026-09-27T16:06:31.154337+00:00] adjudicate-budget-tripped: stopped after 315,063 / 250,000 tokens\\n[2026-09-27T17:32:19.698737+00:00] compiler-flush-failed: memory-compiler flush failed (session 5a33a7ad-69b0-4a38-a3df-3a1b420dd536): FLUSH_ERROR: ResultError: Claude Code returned an error result: You've hit your session limit · resets 12:40pm (America/Chicago) (exit code: 1) | a single failure is usually transient session-end contention (retries exhausted) — check scripts/flush.log; only if it repeats across sessions suspect bundled-CLI version skew — fix: cd ~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler && uv lock --upgrade-package claude-agent-sdk && uv sync\\n[2026-09-27 23:43] daily-backup: 4 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:SecondBrain, repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, repo-behind-blocked:skills, manifest-unmanaged:RunningTheRoom - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (3049 chars, updated 2026-09-28 11:39)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":521},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8143b4eb-4383-408a-977f-55eb116d4fa0","timestamp":"2026-09-28T12:59:29.387Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8143b4eb-4383-408a-977f-55eb116d4fa0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"036443e5-7cb5-4041-a502-54ef5f0d47dd","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nMonday, September 28, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n301 compiled articles (223 concepts, 77 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n# Daily Log: 2026-09-27\\n\\n## Sessions\\n\\n## Memory Maintenance\\n\\n### Memory Flush (12:32)\\n\\nFLUSH_ERROR: ResultError: Claude Code returned an error result: You've hit your session limit \\u00b7 resets 12:40pm (America/Chicago) (exit code: 1)\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":522},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c7e6ef2b-cf44-4dab-9346-83577724c141","timestamp":"2026-09-28T12:59:29.387Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c7e6ef2b-cf44-4dab-9346-83577724c141","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"036443e5-7cb5-4041-a502-54ef5f0d47dd","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":534},"type":"attachment","uuid":"29a22b5b-fb3d-4eec-ae10-c3d3d0faa09f","timestamp":"2026-09-28T12:59:29.400Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"29a22b5b-fb3d-4eec-ae10-c3d3d0faa09f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["<EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>\nYou have superpowers.\n\n**Below is the full content of your 'superpowers:using-superpowers' skill - your introduction to using skills. For all other skills, use the 'Skill' tool:**\n\n---\nname: using-superpowers\ndescription: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring skill invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions\n---\n\n<SUBAGENT-STOP>\nIf you were dispatched as a subagent to execute a specific task, ignore this skill.\n</SUBAGENT-STOP>\n\n<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\n\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\n\nThis is not negotiable. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\n\n## The Rule\n\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action** — including clarifying questions, exploring the codebase, or checking files. If it turns out wrong for the situation, you don't have to use it.\n\n**Before entering plan mode:** if you haven't already brainstormed, invoke the brainstorming skill first.\n\nThen announce \"Using [skill] to [purpose]\" and follow the skill exactly. If it has a checklist, create a todo per item.\n\n## Skill Priority\n\nWhen multiple skills apply, process skills come first — they set the approach, then implementation skills (frontend-design, etc.) carry it out. Brainstorming and systematic-debugging are Superpowers' most common process skills, but the rule holds for any of them.\n\n- \"Let's build X\" → superpowers:brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\n- \"Fix this bug\" → superpowers:systematic-debugging first, then domain skills.\n\n## Red Flags\n\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:\n\n| Thought | Reality |\n|---------|---------|\n| \"This is just a simple question\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\n| \"I need more context first\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\n| \"Let me explore the codebase first\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\n| \"I can check git/files quickly\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\n| \"Let me gather information first\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\n| \"This doesn't need a formal skill\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\n| \"I remember this skill\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\n| \"This doesn't count as a task\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\n| \"The skill is overkill\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\n| \"I'll just do this one thing first\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\n| \"This feels productive\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\n| \"I know what that means\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\n\n## Platform Adaptation\n\nIf your harness appears here, read its reference file for special instructions:\n\n- Claude Code: `references/claude-code-tools.md`\n- Codex: `references/codex-tools.md`\n- Pi: `references/pi-tools.md`\n- Antigravity: `references/antigravity-tools.md`\n- Hermes Agent: `references/hermes-tools.md`\n- Muse: `references/muse-tools.md`\n\n## User Instructions\n\nUser instructions (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md, etc, direct requests) take precedence over skills, which in turn override default behavior. Only skip skill workflows or instructions when your human partner has explicitly told you to.\n</EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>","## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python/R. macOS primary since 2026-08-05; Windows 11 still active. Tool paths: CLAUDE.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \"sharpened, not soothed.\"\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\n- **Status report**: #3 by 9/25, biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: NEXT: phone check; host or local? →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\n- **RTP CLA (9/10)**: NEXT: .ris → Zotero; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla\n- **ATH Tech**: shipped; ITS pending; run 9/29. →Tier A tech-inventory-refresh\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve. Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD → Parquet `athlete-snapshots/` on Drive; backup 21:00; nudges on Win. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. Wk4 COLO: EPA layer only, full profile? →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/22)**: 011 awaits Eric/staff; Jev pilot on draft PR #2, shadow only. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- 