{"parentUuid":"ba92748f-a626-4fe6-bbe6-290156cdefd2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3cc8e953-b179-4ba6-8e84-b08d1ac6669c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# Flint\n\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\npartner. The name comes from Proverbs 27:17 (\"iron sharpens iron\"): the job is to\nsharpen Eric's reasoning, not soothe it.\n\nThis repo holds the knowledge-ingest project that feeds Flint. It is a **side-lane**\nproject (outside the prioritization-slate cap, by Eric's choice on 2026-09-26). No\ncharter. It runs as small background batches during the season.\n\n## The idea\n\nClaude does not learn from files. What makes Flint better is what is stored and\nfindable: Zotero full text, SecondBrain vault notes, and above all **per-discipline\nsynthesis notes** that record where the sources agree, where they disagree, and\nwhere Eric lands. So the job is not \"ingest everything\". It has three layers:\n\n1. **Catalog everything** with a script, spending no tokens (step 0 below).\n2. **Deep-ingest a short ranked list.**\n3. **Synthesize one discipline at a time.** This layer is the thought partner.\n\n## Steps\n\n| Step | What | Tool | State |\n|---|---|---|---|\n(eval):1: === not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F4xRn8wpDABVdK4BJJZfYE"}]},"uuid":"ef2a15aa-1ca9-4178-8e61-34e4312e8ffc","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:05:19.222Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n# Flint\n\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\npartner. The name comes from Proverbs 27:17 (\"iron sharpens iron\"): the job is to\nsharpen Eric's reasoning, not soothe it.\n\nThis repo holds the knowledge-ingest project that feeds Flint. It is a **side-lane**\nproject (outside the prioritization-slate cap, by Eric's choice on 2026-09-26). No\ncharter. It runs as small background batches during the season.\n\n## The idea\n\nClaude does not learn