1CfVtMGzPveBLg989g2TAm","attributionSkill":"dev-sync","type":"assistant","uuid":"39f32c5c-eda9-46bf-9c95-6334a1b4eaf4","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:05:29.977Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"39f32c5c-eda9-46bf-9c95-6334a1b4eaf4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3cc8e953-b179-4ba6-8e84-b08d1ac6669c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0166nDVMTpWZ6gdBFsmgTsfP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/RESEARCH.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"afcda73c-8a46-4c11-8ed9-86146063b612","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:05:30.121Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RESEARCH.md","oldString":"| `LibraryProject/` | Book library → advisor entries → own `CLAUDE.md` |\n","newString":"| `LibraryProject/` | Book library → advisor entries → own `CLAUDE.md` |\n| `Flint/` | Knowledge-ingest side-lane that feeds Flint, the sport-science thought partner: catalog, deep-ingest, per-discipline synthesis. Outside the slate cap → own `CLAUDE.md` |\n","originalFile":"# RESEARCH — area index\n\nLiterature, citation library, and reading pipelines. The grounded-evidence\nlayer behind the applied work.\n\n## Projects\n\n| Folder | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `SportScienceResearchRepo/` | Main research repo. Has `CONTEXT.md`, a spec sheet, and an `index.html` micro-app → own `CLAUDE.md` |\n| `ZoteroInjestion/` | Zotero ingest pipeline (~1,850 files). Note the spelling — \"Injestion\", not \"Ingestion\". |\n| `LibraryProject/` | Book library → advisor entries → own `CLAUDE.md` |\n| `Weekly_Research_Review/` | \"Research in 5\": weekly one-paper review. Deck PDF for Teams, post, email, running index. Outputs on `_DRIVE/07_EDUCATION/Research_in_5` → own `AGENTS.md` |\n| `Epilepsy-Baseball-Research/` | Epilepsy + baseball literature review |\n| `TOS_Evidence_Brief/` | Thoracic outlet syndrome in overhead throwing athletes. One-page briefing note + 14-page evidence review, built to Word/PDF by `scripts/` → own `AGENTS.md` |\n| `BookInbox/` | Staging for books not yet ingested |\n| `reMarkale_extract/` | reMarkable highlight extraction. Note the spelling — \"reMarkale\". |\n| `ContextVault/` | Context storage experiment |\n| `May_Meetings_Research/` | May 2026 meeting materials and EOY research reporting. Disk is the source of truth → own `CLAUDE.md`. Dormant. |\n\n## Tooling that serves this area\n\n- Skills: `sports-science-research-grounding`, `library-advisor`,\n  `ingest-book`, `ingest-resource`, `pp-zotero-research-library`\n- CLIs: `zotero-research-library-pp-cli`, `zotero-research-library-pp-mcp`\n- MCP: `zotero` (the one server in local `~/.claude.json`)\n- Vault: `~/SecondBrain` holds 842 notes and has its own `CLAUDE.md`\n- Compiled knowledge: `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/` (185 articles)\n\n## Notes\n\n- Search across everything with `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n  rather than reading the knowledge index directly.\n- Zotero recall gotcha: `project_milvus-lock-misdiagnosis.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":6,"newStart":10,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `SportScienceResearchRepo/` | Main research repo. Has `CONTEXT.md`, a spec sheet, and an `index.html` micro-app → own `CLAUDE.md` |"," | `ZoteroInjestion/` | Zotero ingest pipeline (~1,850 files). Note the spelling — \"Injestion\", not \"Ingestion\". |"," | `LibraryProject/` | Book library → advisor entries → own `CLAUDE.md` |","+| `Flint/` | Knowledge-ingest side-lane that feeds Flint, the sport-science thought partner: catalog, deep-ingest, per-discipline synthesis. Outside the slate cap → own `CLAUDE.md` |"," | `Weekly_Research_Review/` | \"Research in 5\": weekly one-paper review. Deck PDF for Teams, post, email, running index. Outputs on `_DRIVE/07_EDUCATION/Research_in_5` → own `AGENTS.md` |"," | `Epilepsy-Baseball-Research/` | Epilepsy + baseball literature review |"," | `TOS_Evidence_Brief/` | Thoracic outlet syndrome in overhead throwing athletes. One-page briefing note + 14-page evidence review, built to Word/PDF by `scripts/` → own `AGENTS.md` |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39f32c5c-eda9-46bf-9c95-6334a1b4eaf4","session_id":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"afcda73c-8a46-4c11-8ed9-86146063b612","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfVtMHPiapTEiuBN5KC1h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K1EJ5Ca1cgLaQL7eaWsvHy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add RESEARCH.md && git commit -qm \"RESEARCH router: add Flint\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XvdR3JgNUAww239duJui4w\" && git push -q 2>&1 | tail -2; git status -sb | head -1\necho '--- AGENTS'; sed -n 1,40p TypeSafe_Sandbox/AGENTS.md; echo '--- STATUS'; cat TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/STATUS.md | head -80; echo '--- handoffs'; ls -t TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/handoffs | head -3","description":"Commit router fix and read TypeSafe context"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":248,"cache_read_input_tokens":90553,"output_tokens":637,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":248,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":90553,"cache_creation_input_tokens":248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":248},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01K1EJ5Ca1cgLaQL7eaWsvHy":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV && git add RESEARCH.md && git commit -qm \"RESEARCH router: add Flint\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XvdR3JgNUAww239duJui4w\" && git push -q 2>&1 | tail -2; git status -sb | head -1\necho '--- AGENTS'; sed -n 1,40p TypeSafe_Sandbox/AGENTS.md; echo '--- STATUS'; cat TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/STATUS.md | head -80; echo '--- handoffs'; ls -t TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/handoffs | head -3","description":"Commit router fix and read TypeSafe context"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01K1EJ5Ca1cgLaQL7eaWsvHy":{"cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfVtMGzPveBLg989g2TAm","attributionSkill":"dev-sync","type":"assistant","uuid":"81c4d047-f4db-4ad3-9734-abf812f871f3","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:05:32.621Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"81c4d047-f4db-4ad3-9734-abf812f871f3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3cc8e953-b179-4ba6-8e84-b08d1ac6669c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1EJ5Ca1cgLaQL7eaWsvHy","type":"tool_result","content":"hint: 'git pull' before pushing again.\nhint: See the 'Note about fast-forwards' in 'git push --help' for details.\n## main...origin/main [ahead 1]\n--- AGENTS\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: TypeSafe_Sandbox\n\n## What this is\nA sandbox for building against the TypeSafe System One API (the Jev model), which\nreturns typed judgments and probabilities instead of generated text. The API key is\nNOT stored in this repo; see Secrets below for where it lives on each machine.\n`setup_global_key.sh` installs the macOS side once per machine. `smoke_test.py` proves\nthe key resolves and the API answers.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n\n## Secrets\n- Never paste the API key into a chat session. Claude Code transcripts under\n  `~/.claude/projects/*.jsonl` are tracked in the `dotclaude` repo and pushed nightly.\n- Never put the key in `~/.claude/settings.json` or `settings.local.json`. Both are tracked.\n- The key has one home per machine, and nothing about it syncs between them:\n  - macOS: the Keychain, service name `typesafe-api-key`, installed by `setup_global_key.sh`.\n  - Windows: `~/.claude/typesafe.env`, which the dotclaude whitelist auto-ignores.\n- The key is 108 characters and starts with `apikey_`. Dropping that prefix returns 401.\n--- STATUS\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.\n- **2026-09-26 (answer-key audit step)**: added to `docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md` as a\n  required step in every pre-registered test: Eric blind-judges Jev's confident\n  disagreements with the labels (max 20), and both scores are reported. The original\n  labels still decide pass or fail. Prompted by the \"Just Ask Jev\" paper (arXiv\n  2609.29429), which found label defects in 3 benchmarks, as we did in 3 write-ups.\n  The rest of that paper (give Jev the source, calibrate thresholds, act only on\n  confident answers) was already practice here. Open, Eric's call: a pre-registered\n  test of Jev checking course summaries against their transcripts, only if someone\n  other than Eric reads those summaries.\n- **2026-09-22 (doctor-plus cleanup)**: Router test fixed. Sports scores now route to `pp-espn` (#27), and ALL CHECKS PASSED. CreateSkill was dropped from the expected-skill lists and the roster rebuilt and installed (127 skills). The Mac still needs `build_roster.py` then `install.py`. The four old worktrees were removed. 8 gitignored `private/` files that existed only in them (fireflies/notes/spring probe sheets and Jev runs) were saved into the main checkout.\n- **2026-09-22 (spring exit notes → trajectory, CLOSED)**: **FAILS by 0.002, the ninth\n  item measured off the map.** Pre-registered in `93c4120` (weights, cut points and\n  both bars fixed before the first call). Composite of four department Scores vs\n  blended snaps: **rho 0.298** against a **0.30** bar (n 34, p 0.087); Claude pass\n  0.352, keyword rubric 0.218. **Stability rho 0.998** over two runs of all 99 (bar\n  0.95), 96/99 same bin, 0 failures. At n=34 the CI is about ±0.33, so 0.298 and 0.352\n  cannot be separated, but a near-miss is still a miss and the bar was not moved. The\n  Claude pass stays and `coach_pdf.py` is untouched. **The finding worth keeping is\n  role, not trajectory:** the held-out role Score hits **rho 0.643** (n 34), and the\n  assumption that role is just extraction is wrong, and was checked — only 5 of 99\n  notes carry a literal \"Role =\", and role words anywhere in the coach note settle\n  16/34 at rho 0.405 (n.s.) where Jev reaches 0.664 on the same 16. That is post-hoc on\n  the same athletes, so it earns **its own pre-registered test against 2026 snaps**\n  once a fresh `pff.db` lands, not a retroactive pass. Write-up:\n  `docs/SPRING_NOTES_TRAJECTORY.md`.\n- **2026-09-22 (Fireflies meeting → project, BUILT and SHIPPED)**: the **first item to\n  pass its pre-registered test** after seven kills. Blind on 40 meetings, Jev was\n  confident on 36/39 and right on 33/36 (bars 60% and 90%); the keyword baseline was\n  right on 1 of 12. **The pass rests mostly on \"none of these\" (27/28).** On real\n  project meetings it was **7 of 11**, and OKRs_2026-27 was the repeat miss (its\n  portfolio purpose is one line). Shipped as `meeting-sync` step 4\n  (`scripts/tag_project.py`) with `meeting-prep` reading the tag: **claude-skills PR #1\n  MERGED** (`2da77af`) and pulled live on Windows; **the Mac needs `git pull` in\n  `~/.claude/skills`**. Backfill over the vault the same day: 246 notes marked, **14\n  tagged**, 206 confident \"none\", 26 unsure, 260 lines added and **0 removed**\n  (SecondBrain `43ef103`). Append-only, fails open, one `jev-project` marker per note.\n  Not done: the Mac run, and rewriting the OKRs purpose (that must be judged on\n  meetings after 2026-09-17, not these 40). Write-up: `docs/FIREFLIES_PROJECT_TAG.md`.\n- **2026-09-22 (permission gate + sensitive routing, use cases 1 and 9, CLOSED)**:\n  **both measured off the map, the eighth in a row.** Pre-registered in `f27c90b`\n  (bar amended before labeling in `bcf9ced`). 2,808 gated calls from 50 Windows\n  transcripts; residue 62%, mostly script bodies the sanitizer strips. **Use case 9:\n  code only.** 0 of 20 egress calls carried health data the path rule missed; the 5 L1\n  blocks are folder names in prose (v2 fix: match paths, not words). **Use case 1:\n  Eric labeled all 40 blind rows `run`; Jev agreed on 17 (0.42 against a 0.80 bar)\n  and would have asked on 23 of 40 safe calls**, mostly scripts and outward MCP calls\n  it cannot read. Gate stays code only. **Shadow hook INSTALLED on Windows**\n  (log-only, never blocks, no network) at `~/.claude/permission-gate/shadow.jsonl`,\n  so any real risky call the rules miss shows up there. Not on the Mac yet. Write-up:\n  `docs/PERMISSION_GATE_MEASUREMENT.md`.\n- **2026-09-22 (conditional context, CLOSED)**: use case 7 from Diogo Almeida's\n  \"TypeSafe + coding agent\" notes (topic-routed rules, the @0xcodila post) was\n  **measured off the map, the seventh in a row.** Only two rules are missing from\n  sub-project sessions: department names and a pointer to `baylor_docstyle`, together\n  about 110 tokens. Frozen cwd+keyword baseline on 30 real prompts from a\n  TypeSafe-heavy two-day Windows sample: recall **1 of 2** (7% base rate, a fact\n  about that sample, not the workload); the hit was luck (\"send\"), and the miss is\n  catchable from the file written. Always-loading beats any router at that size.\n  **Eric's call:** add the three department names to global `USER.md` via\n  `/memory-write`. Write-up:\n  `docs/CONDITIONAL_CONTEXT_MEASUREMENT.md`. Other nine use cases in the post: out of\n  reach without owning the harness, already built (skill router), or ruled out by the\n  map (model routing). Permission gate and sensitive routing were then measured; see above.\n- **2026-09-21 (surgery notes, CLOSED)**: pre-registered test **FAILS** — Jev 75% on\n  the regex-settled notes (bar 90%), though 12/15 on the ambiguous ones (bar 11).\n  Seventh item measured off the map. **The finding that matters is not about Jev:** the\n  annual report's \"17 undocumented completed surgeries\" is **22** under Eric's blind\n  labels, and only 14 of the regex's 17 hold. Jev found 21 of 22 (regex 14), but at ~60\n  notes a year a human read wins. **Eric's rule (09-21): only surgeries within 12 months of the note count**, so 22 is not final: code hints 9 within / 5 older / 8 unclear; Eric marks Y/N tomorrow in `notes_probe/private/recent_sheet.md`. Write-up:\n  `docs/SURGERY_NOTES_PROBE.md`. Fireflies attendee baseline also added\n  (`docs/FIREFLIES_ATTENDEE_BASELINE.md`, 6% settle). Next under option A: spring exit\n  notes (#3).\n- **2026-09-21 (Evidence Library tags, CLOSED)**: Eric's blind check came back **Jev 12,\n  rules 8** (60%, bar 70%). **The rules stay**; nothing written back. Sixth item in a row\n--- handoffs\n2026-09-21-rerank-measured-and-ri5-002-verified.md\n2026-09-21-leverage-sweep-all-projects.md\n2026-09-20-prose-numbers-and-jev-scoping.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ad26e8b7-0db2-4284-8903-36279325714a","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:05:33.916Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"hint: 'git pull' before pushing again.\nhint: See the 'Note about fast-forwards' in 'git push --help' for details.\n## main...origin/main [ahead 1]\n--- AGENTS\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: TypeSafe_Sandbox\n\n## What this is\nA sandbox for building against the TypeSafe System One API (the Jev model), which\nreturns typed judgments and probabilities instead of generated text. The API key is\nNOT stored in this repo; see Secrets below for where it lives on each machine.\n`setup_global_key.sh` installs the macOS side once per machine. `smoke_test.py` proves\nthe key resolves and the API answers.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n\n## Secrets\n- Never paste the API key into a chat session. Claude Code transcripts under\n  `~/.claude/projects/*.jsonl` are tracked in the `dotclaude` repo and pushed nightly.\n- Never put the key in `~/.claude/settings.json` or `settings.local.json`. Both are tracked.\n- The key has one home per machine, and nothing about it syncs between them:\n  - macOS: the Keychain, service name `typesafe-api-key`, installed by `setup_global_key.sh`.\n  - Windows: `~/.claude/typesafe.env`, which the dotclaude whitelist auto-ignores.\n- The key is 108 characters and starts with `apikey_`. Dropping that prefix returns 401.\n--- STATUS\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.\n- **2026-09-26 (answer-key audit step)**: added to `docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md` as a\n  required step in every pre-registered test: Eric blind-judges Jev's confident\n  disagreements with the labels (max 20), and both scores are reported. The original\n  labels still decide pass or fail. Prompted by the \"Just Ask Jev\" paper (arXiv\n  2609.29429), which found label defects in 3 benchmarks, as we did in 3 write-ups.\n  The rest of that paper (give Jev the source, calibrate thresholds, act only on\n  confident answers) was already practice here. Open, Eric's call: a pre-registered\n  test of Jev checking course summaries against their transcripts, only if someone\n  other than Eric reads those summaries.\n- **2026-09-22 (doctor-plus cleanup)**: Router test fixed. Sports scores now route to `pp-espn` (#27), and ALL CHECKS PASSED. CreateSkill was dropped from the expected-skill lists and the roster rebuilt and installed (127 skills). The Mac still needs `build_roster.py` then `install.py`. The four old worktrees were removed. 8 gitignored `private/` files that existed only in them (fireflies/notes/spring probe sheets and Jev runs) were saved into the main checkout.\n- **2026-09-22 (spring exit notes → trajectory, CLOSED)**: **FAILS by 0.002, the ninth\n  item measured off the map.** Pre-registered in `93c4120` (weights, cut points and\n  both bars fixed before the first call). Composite of four department Scores vs\n  blended snaps: **rho 0.298** against a **0.30** bar (n 34, p 0.087); Claude pass\n  0.352, keyword rubric 0.218. **Stability rho 0.998** over two runs of all 99 (bar\n  0.95), 96/99 same bin, 0 failures. At n=34 the CI is about ±0.33, so 0.298 and 0.352\n  cannot be separated, but a near-miss is still a miss and the bar was not moved. The\n  Claude pass stays and `coach_pdf.py` is untouched. **The finding worth keeping is\n  role, not trajectory:** the held-out role Score hits **rho 0.643** (n 34), and the\n  assumption that role is just extraction is wrong, and was checked — only 5 of 99\n  notes carry a literal \"Role =\", and role words anywhere in the coach note settle\n  16/34 at rho 0.405 (n.s.) where Jev reaches 0.664 on the same 16. That is post-hoc on\n  the same athletes, so it earns **its own pre-registered test against 2026 snaps**\n  once a fresh `pff.db` lands, not a retroactive pass. Write-up:\n  `docs/SPRING_NOTES_TRAJECTORY.md`.\n- **2026-09-22 (Fireflies meeting → project, BUILT and SHIPPED)**: the **first item to\n  pass its pre-registered test** after seven kills. Blind on 40 meetings, Jev was\n  confident on 36/39 and right on 33/36 (bars 60% and 90%); the keyword baseline was\n  right on 1 of 12. **The pass rests mostly on \"none of these\" (27/28).** On real\n  project meetings it was **7 of 11**, and OKRs_2026-27 was the repeat miss (its\n  portfolio purpose is one line). Shipped as `meeting-sync` step 4\n  (`scripts/tag_project.py`) with `meeting-prep` reading the tag: **claude-skills PR #1\n  MERGED** (`2da77af`) and pulled live on Windows; **the Mac needs `git pull` in\n  `~/.claude/skills`**. Backfill over the vault the same day: 246 notes marked, **14\n  tagged**, 206 confident \"none\", 26 unsure, 260 lines added and **0 removed**\n  (SecondBrain `43ef103`). Append-only, fails open, one `jev-project` marker per note.\n  Not done: the Mac run, and rewriting the OKRs purpose (that must be judged on\n  meetings after 2026-09-17, not these 40). Write-up: `docs/FIREFLIES_PROJECT_TAG.md`.\n- **2026-09-22 (permission gate + sensitive routing, use cases 1 and 9, CLOSED)**:\n  **both measured off the map, the eighth in a row.** Pre-registered in `f27c90b`\n  (bar amended before labeling in `bcf9ced`). 2,808 gated calls from 50 Windows\n  transcripts; residue 62%, mostly script bodies the sanitizer strips. **Use case 9:\n  code only.** 0 of 20 egress calls carried health data the path rule missed; the 5 L1\n  blocks are folder names in prose (v2 fix: match paths, not words). **Use case 1:\n  Eric labeled all 40 blind rows `run`; Jev agreed on 17 (0.42 against a 0.80 bar)\n  and would have asked on 23 of 40 safe calls**, mostly scripts and outward MCP calls\n  it cannot read. Gate stays code only. **Shadow hook INSTALLED on Windows**\n  (log-only, never blocks, no network) at `~/.claude/permission-gate/shadow.jsonl`,\n  so any real risky call the rules miss shows up there. Not on the Mac yet. Write-up:\n  `docs/PERMISSION_GATE_MEASUREMENT.md`.\n- **2026-09-22 (conditional context, CLOSED)**: use case 7 from Diogo Almeida's\n  \"TypeSafe + coding agent\" notes (topic-routed rules, the @0xcodila post) was\n  **measured off the map, the seventh in a row.** Only two rules are missing from\n  sub-project sessions: department names and a pointer to `baylor_docstyle`, together\n  about 110 tokens. Frozen cwd+keyword baseline on 30 real prompts from a\n  TypeSafe-heavy two-day Windows sample: recall **1 of 2** (7% base rate, a fact\n  about that sample, not the workload); the hit was luck (\"send\"), and the miss is\n  catchable from the file written. Always-loading beats any router at that size.\n  **Eric's call:** add the three department names to global `USER.md` via\n  `/memory-write`. Write-up:\n  `docs/CONDITIONAL_CONTEXT_MEASUREMENT.md`. Other nine use cases in the post: out of\n  reach without owning the harness, already built (skill router), or ruled out by the\n  map (model routing). Permission gate and sensitive routing were then measured; see above.\n- **2026-09-21 (surgery notes, CLOSED)**: pre-registered test **FAILS** — Jev 75% on\n  the regex-settled notes (bar 90%), though 12/15 on the ambiguous ones (bar 11).\n  Seventh item measured off the map. **The finding that matters is not about Jev:** the\n  annual report's \"17 undocumented completed surgeries\" is **22** under Eric's blind\n  labels, and only 14 of the regex's 17 hold. Jev found 21 of 22 (regex 14), but at ~60\n  notes a year a human read wins. **Eric's rule (09-21): only surgeries within 12 months of the note count**, so 22 is not final: code hints 9 within / 5 older / 8 unclear; Eric marks Y/N tomorrow in `notes_probe/private/recent_sheet.md`. Write-up:\n  `docs/SURGERY_NOTES_PROBE.md`. Fireflies attendee baseline also added\n  (`docs/FIREFLIES_ATTENDEE_BASELINE.md`, 6% settle). Next under option A: spring exit\n  notes (#3).\n- **2026-09-21 (Evidence Library tags, CLOSED)**: Eric's blind check came back **Jev 12,\n  rules 8** (60%, bar 70%). **The rules stay**; nothing written back. Sixth item in a row\n--- handoffs\n2026-09-21-rerank-measured-and-ri5-002-verified.md\n2026-09-21-leverage-sweep-all-projects.md\n2026-09-20-prose-numbers-and-jev-scoping.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81c4d047-f4db-4ad3-9734-abf812f871f3","session_id":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
