Merge conflict in RESEARCH.md\nAutomatic merge failed; fix conflicts and then commit the result.\nhint: use 'git pull' before pushing again.\nhint: See the 'Note about fast-forwards' in 'git push --help' for details.\n## main...origin/main [ahead 1, behind 11]\nM  FOOTBALL.md\nM  PROGRAM.md\nUU RESEARCH.md\n365:## Next\n366-- **Watch the shadow log** (`~/.claude/permission-gate/shadow.jsonl`, Windows). After\n367-  a week or two, count `residue` and look for any real risky call the code rules\n368-  missed. That is the only evidence left that could reopen a Jev gate. Cheap first\n369-  win: a v2 `rules.py` (quoted `cd`, `uv run`, `echo` headers, `git -C`, and L1 on\n370-  path arguments only), pre-registered as a new rule set.\n371-- **Mac:** copy `permission_gate/{shadow_hook.py,rules.py,sanitize.py}` into\n419:## Open questions\n420-- **API key per machine (moved here from the DEV `PLATFORM.md` router, 2026-09-22):** both machines have a key as of 2026-09-19. Windows is verified end to end against the live API; the Mac key is added but not yet verified. Run `smoke_test.py` on the Mac to close this.\n421-- **Spring exit notes (#3) or maintenance mode?** Recommended: stop, TypeSafe to maintenance (router + Zotero classify + verifier kept). Seven items measured off the map in a row. Eric's call.\n422-- ANSWERED 2026-09-20: **governance is no longer a blocker on Jev work.** Eric\n423-  cleared Option C (\"we can send whatever we need to typesafe\") and separately\n424-  cleared the Telemetry third-party-processing question. Noted for the record that","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/FOOTBALL.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":7,"newStart":11,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `CFB_Victory_Model/` | Weekly prediction model. Capture cadence and rules: `/forecast-capture`, `project_cfb-forecast-capture.md`. |"," | `CFB_Forecast_Archive/` | Read-only copies of the weekly forecast freezes, by year. Source of truth stays in `CFB_Victory_Model/data/`. |"," | `PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/` | Player profile build → own `CLAUDE.md` |","-| `PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/` | 2021–2025 Baylor offensive play-call charting CSVs (PFF export) **+ the Phase 1 self-scout**, joined to `Football/PFF_Data_Project/data/pff.db` (read-only) at 99.3%. Own `CLAUDE.md` + `AGENTS.md`. Private repo. Finding: success rate 57.4% → 49.5%, concentrated on 1st & 10 and the run game. **Only 2024–2025 carry outcome columns**; 2021–2023 cannot support success rate at all. Phase 1 has no EPA — that needs CFBD and is Phase 2. |","+| `PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA/` | 2021–2025 Baylor offensive play-call charting CSVs (PFF export) **+ the Phase 1 self-scout**, joined to PFF data (read-only) at 99.3%. Own `CLAUDE.md` + `AGENTS.md`. Private repo. Finding: success rate 57.4% → 49.5%, concentrated on 1st & 10 and the run game. **Only 2024–2025 carry outcome columns**; 2021–2023 cannot support success rate at all. Phase 1 has no EPA — that needs CFBD and is Phase 2. |"," | `2025-11-25_EOS_Football_Analysis_GPS_ERR/` | End-of-season GPS + PFF performance analysis (2024 vs 2025 seasons). 2024-2025 analysis complete: executive report, coach materials, visualizations. Own `CLAUDE.md` + `docs/`. Git repo. **Disk is the source of truth; the Claude cloud project \"Post Season Analysis - Baylor Football\" is only a pointer to it.** FERPA data. |"," | `PostSesaonAnalysis/` | Duplicate scaffold of the EOS GPS analysis from an earlier upload. Not the working copy — fold in or archive. |"," | `Game_Tracker_PWA/` | Football game tracking PWA for the coaching staff (`football-tracker-pwa/`). Own `AGENTS.md` + `docs/STATUS.md`. Git repo, pushed to erash11. Disk is the source of truth; the Claude cloud project `WebApps` is only a pointer. |"]},{"oldStart":28,"oldLines":7,"newStart":28,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `FaceComps/` | Face-comparison work. Carries its own graph output folder. |"," | `PFF_Data_Project/` | PFF data ingest and analysis. `outputs/` holds the finished reports (per-snap game demands, positional speed/collision thresholds) plus their `PROC_*.csv` working tables. |"," | `MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/` | Week-by-week 2026 opponent matchup analysis. Own `CLAUDE.md` + `docs/`. Git repo. Source of truth for the project; the Claude cloud project is only a pointer to it. |","-| `PlayerPersonel/` | Player personnel film review (first case: Jacorey Thomas). Python + extracted frames. Moved from `~/Documents/ChatGPT/` on 2026-09-07. **`git init` with zero commits — nothing is versioned yet.** |","+| `PlayerPersonel/` | Player personnel film review (first case: Jacorey Thomas). Python + extracted frames. Moved from `~/Documents/ChatGPT/` on 2026-09-07. Own private GitHub repo. |"," | `SpeedProfiling/` | Speed profiling |"," | `PlayerEvals/` | Player evaluations |"," | `SpringPlayerEvals_SymAnalysis/` | Spring evals + symmetry analysis |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PROGRAM.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":6,"newStart":31,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Folder | What it is |"," |---|---|"," | `Department_Audits/` | Executable sport performance departmental audit playbooks → own `AGENTS.md` + `docs/context.md`. Disk is the source of truth; the Cowork project is only a pointer. Bulk source materials still live in Google Drive. |","+| `RunningTheRoom/` | Old Bull Performance \"Running The Room\" course (Jason Weber) distilled into a department operating plan and staff-development recommendations. Private repo; course media and PDFs stay on Drive at `09_PRO_DEV/Old bull performance`. |"," | `SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework/` | Software and tech management framework |"," | `Sport_Tech_Vetting/` | Vetting process for sport tech vendors |"," | `Transformative_Athlete_Experience/` | Athlete experience initiative |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RESEARCH.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":7,"newStart":10,"newLines":11,"lines":[" | `SportScienceResearchRepo/` | Main research repo. Has `CONTEXT.md`, a spec sheet, and an `index.html` micro-app → own `CLAUDE.md` |"," | `ZoteroInjestion/` | Zotero ingest pipeline (~1,850 files). Note the spelling — \"Injestion\", not \"Ingestion\". |"," | `LibraryProject/` | Book library → advisor entries → own `CLAUDE.md` |","+<<<<<<< HEAD"," | `Flint/` | Knowledge-ingest side-lane that feeds Flint, the sport-science thought partner: catalog, deep-ingest, per-discipline synthesis. Outside the slate cap → own `CLAUDE.md` |","+=======","+| `Flint/` | Knowledge base behind Claude-as-\"Flint\", Eric's sport-science thought partner (side lane). Drive catalog, own-method baseline, triage, per-discipline synthesis. Plan in `docs/PLAN.md` → own `AGENTS.md` |","+>>>>>>> origin/main"," | `Weekly_Research_Review/` | \"Research in 5\": weekly one-paper review. Deck PDF for Teams, post, email, running index. Outputs on `_DRIVE/07_EDUCATION/Research_in_5` → own `AGENTS.md` |"," | `Epilepsy-Baseball-Research/` | Epilepsy + baseball literature review |"," | `TOS_Evidence_Brief/` | Thoracic outlet syndrome in overhead throwing athletes. One-page briefing note + 14-page evidence review, built to Word/PDF by `scripts/` → own `AGENTS.md` |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1,"newLines":45,"lines":[" # STATUS — ~/DEV workspace root"," "," ## Current state","+- 2026-09-26 (Codex hook diagnosis): The `codex@openai-codex` cached plugin's","+  SessionEnd hook already declares the platform's 3-second cap, but its broker","+  shutdown socket previously had no reply timeout. Added a 500 ms socket timeout","+  in the local plugin cache; a deliberately silent broker returned in 204 ms,","+  and a no-broker SessionEnd smoke test exited 0 in 386 ms. This cache edit may","+  be replaced by a plugin refresh. The running session's earlier clamp warning","+  remains historical until restart. The 11-warning list is not fully available;","+  screenshots confirm skill-context overflow (303 skills omitted) and a","+  WebSocket-to-HTTPS fallback. `codex doctor` separately finds missing MCP env","+  vars for github/node_repl, plus environment and thread-inventory warnings.","+- 2026-09-26 (Windows): Found the SecondBrain checkout at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\SecondBrain`.","+  Pushed SCN sprint-course commits `23d0ad0` and `41a7f8d` after merging the remote","+  weekly-slate update; `origin/main` now contains both and the checkout is clean.","+- 2026-09-26 closeout resume: all 147 scanned DEV repos and the three shared config","+  repos are clean and pushed. The Sep 25 research handoff is committed. The dev-docs","+  harvest succeeded; the memory index retry hit its 600-second timeout after the","+  `ENOBUFS` buffer fix. Detail is in the research handoff addendum.","+- 2026-09-25 (Windows, SportScienceResearchRepo): pulled and audited the Health & Performance","+  Evidence Library, screened shortlist positions 1-6, excluded one editorial, and published","+  five source-reviewed papers as Batch 18 (712 total, next ID 744). Regenerated the","+  96-candidate shortlist, refreshed stale repo status/roadmap pointers, and pushed. The","+  Ask the Library concierge pilot tooling passes tests, but this checkout has no real","+  pilot requests, briefs, feedback, audits, or scorecard. The next Ask implementation","+  direction awaits Eric's choice between the staff pilot and automated generation.","+  Closeout handoff: `SportScienceResearchRepo/docs/handoffs/2026-09-25-evidence-library-batch18-ask-library.md`.","+- 2026-09-24 (cloud): Decided against moving the DuckDB files and API pulls to Supabase.","+  Plan instead: raw pulls to a data tier under `_DRIVE` on the primary storage drive, each","+  machine rebuilds its local `.duckdb` from them, Drive versioning is the backup. Nothing","+  executed yet; the checklist needs a machine with the repos on disk. Detail:","+  `docs/handoffs/2026-09-24-data-tier-for-duckdb-and-pulls.md`.","+- 2026-09-23 (Windows, dev-sync): all 143 discovered project repos were fetched, merged,","+  pushed, and verified clean. Incoming work landed in `CFB_Victory_Model` (4 commits),","+  `CFB_Forecast_Archive` (2), and the DEV `claude-global-memory` checkout (4). No project","+  clone or repo creation was needed. Shared skills synced to both Windows agent views.","+  Today's global-memory transcript conflict was merged with both machines' entries kept.","+  The failing Claude Code `PreToolUse` hook came from a hard-coded Mac `dcg` path in shared","+  `~/.claude/settings.json`; the duplicate was removed and pushed as `2cd9fa2`.","+  `FOOTBALL.md` was corrected for the relocated PFF database and the versioned","+  `PlayerPersonel` repo."," - 2026-09-22 (Windows, doctor-plus): context audit against the 6 context-engineering shifts. Everything is merged and live. The knowledge-base injection was cut from 20KB to 3.8KB by a memory-compiler pull (Windows was 6 behind). skill-creator is now the one authoring skill; CreateSkill is deleted. A CLAUDE.md line outranks the superpowers \"1% rule\". Router state moved into project STATUS files. Detail: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-doctor-plus-context-audit.md`."," - 2026-09-22 (Windows): Closed out the 09-21 handoffs. All leftover worktrees cleared from `_INBOX`,","   `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` and `DEV` — one of them (`status+closeout-0917`) held an unmerged 09-17"]},{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":6,"newStart":70,"newLines":18,"lines":[" - Baylor's 2026 forecast snapshot is frozen at 4.49 expected wins."," "," ## Next","+- Codex: after a fresh session, check whether SessionEnd completes without a","+  timeout and inspect the remaining warning screens. Reduce duplicate plugin","+  skill bundles only after choosing which ones should stay available; the","+  skill-context overflow is separate from hook execution. Carry the broker","+  timeout fix into the plugin source or reapply it after cache refresh.","+- Recheck memsearch incremental indexing; the Sep 25 error remains in","+  `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` and the retry timed out.","+- SportScienceResearchRepo: screen Batch 19 from its refreshed queue. For Ask the Library,","+  run the approved staff pilot or define the agent build target after Eric's direction.","+- Run the data-tier checklist in `docs/handoffs/2026-09-24-data-tier-for-duckdb-and-pulls.md`: inventory every `.duckdb`/`.db` in DEV first, then gitignore, `build_db`, and the `_DRIVE/03_DATA` move. Windows stops Drive-backing `Desktop\\DEV` only after the data has moved.","+- Restart any Claude Code session that still shows the old `dcg` hook error, then confirm","+  a new Bash or PowerShell tool call runs without a `PreToolUse` error."," - Windows: restart RStudio before the next `Football/SpeedProfiling` session, so it picks up `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT` and does not rebuild the renv library inside DEV."," - Windows: recheck the Google Drive error count (expect 2, was 162). Quit and reopen Drive to force a rescan."," - Next session: confirm every listed skill shows a description (skill listing budget is ~30,000 chars; predicted ~26,800)."]},{"oldStart":44,"oldLines":6,"newStart":95,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - On the Mac, pull `~/.claude/skills` and run its guarded sync so the Mac-generated views receive the same canonical revision."," "," ## Open questions","+- Whether an already-running Claude Code session reloads changed hook settings without a restart."," - Turn off the `last30days` plugin? 0 uses since 2026-08-05."," - Has the exposed VALD client secret been revoked and replaced?"," - `LibraryProject.code-workspace` points at a nonexistent nested `SportScienceResearchRepo`; the live repo is at the DEV root."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/handoffs/2026-09-24-data-tier-for-duckdb-and-pulls.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":137,"lines":["+# 2026-09-24 — Shared data tier for DuckDB files and API pulls (not done; plan)","+","+## What this is","+","+Eric asked whether the datasets that live on the Mac (the DuckDB files, the other database files,","+and the raw API pulls behind them) should move to Supabase so the Windows machine can reach them","+and they are backed up in the cloud. This handoff records the decision and the checklist. **Nothing","+below has been executed.** It was written from a cloud session that could see only the thin `DEV`","+router repo, not the project repos, so every project-specific item must be re-verified on a machine","+that has the repos on disk.","+","+## Decision","+","+- **No Supabase.** The files are DuckDB; Supabase is Postgres. Moving them means migrating every","+  table, rewriting every pipeline to talk to Postgres over the network, and paying latency on every","+  query. The two Supabase projects that already exist (`vald-explorer`, `bookvault`) are both paused","+  as INACTIVE, which is what the free tier does after a week idle. That is a preview of how a pipeline","+  run a few times a week would go.","+- **Raw pulls are the source of truth, not the `.duckdb` files.** Pulls land on the primary storage","+  drive (Google Drive) as Parquet or CSV, date-partitioned. Each machine rebuilds its own local","+  `.duckdb` from them. The `.duckdb` file is a build artifact and never syncs.","+- **DuckDB never opens a file that sits in a Drive-synced folder.** DuckDB and SQLite write in place","+  and hold locks. Drive copying a file mid-write corrupts it or spawns \"conflicted copy\" duplicates.","+- **Backup is Drive versioning** (30 days of file versions) plus the existing `dailybackup` Drive","+  tier. No new backup system.","+- **MotherDuck, not Supabase, if a hosted database is ever wanted.** It is DuckDB in the cloud","+  (`ATTACH 'md:'`), no schema migration, no pipeline rewrite. External service, so only for datasets","+  with no athlete-identifiable data. Not needed for the two-machine problem.","+- **Supabase earns its place only for serving**: a Streamlit dashboard or coach PWA that must read","+  live data from a server, or concurrent access by other staff. Separate decision.","+","+## What is wrong with the current setup","+","+1. **Windows live-syncs DuckDB files through Google Drive.** Drive for Desktop backs up all of","+   `Desktop\\DEV` on Windows. The 09-22 handoff already names the long-term fix as not done: move","+   non-regenerable data to `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive` and stop backing up DEV. Any","+   `.duckdb` or `.db` a pipeline writes inside DEV on Windows is being copied while it is open.","+   The Mac side is safer (the `dailybackup` launchd job is an rsync on a schedule) but can still","+   catch a file mid-write.","+2. **No cross-machine data root.** Both machines already have a `_DRIVE` link inside DEV pointing at","+   the primary storage drive (Mac `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`,","+   Windows `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive`). DexaProject, CATES data, and the PP_Recruiting","+   outputs already use it. What is missing is a data tier under it and pipelines that read and write","+   there instead of a project-local `data/`.","+3. **Both machines can write and nothing says who wins.** Pulls run on the Mac via launchd","+   (afternoon pulls may run late when the Mac sleeps); the large data folders sit on Windows","+   (`Risk_Stratification_Engine/outputs` 1.8 GB, `Football/SpeedProfiling/data` 1.7 GB,","+   `ForcePlate_DecisionSystem/data` 1.6 GB). Two writers on one `.duckdb` will diverge.","+","+## Target layout","+","+```","+_DRIVE/03_DATA/                       # one folder per project, name matches the DEV folder","+  <project>/","+    raw/<source>/<YYYY-MM-DD>.parquet # one file per pull; never rewritten, only added","+    exports/                          # DuckDB EXPORT DATABASE output, for state raw cannot rebuild","+    README.md                         # what the source is, which script pulls it, sensitivity tag","+```","+","+Check what numbering `00_Primary_Storage_Drive` already uses before creating `03_DATA`","+(`00_INBOX` and `02_SPORTS` exist). If the data is sport-specific it may belong under `02_SPORTS`","+instead; pick one and record it in `PERFORMANCE.md` and `FOOTBALL.md`.","+","+Rules that go with it:","+","+- The `.duckdb` file lives on local disk inside the project (gitignored), never under `_DRIVE`.","+- A pull script writes only to `raw/`. It is idempotent by date so either machine can run it and","+  the two never conflict.","+- A `build_db` script (name it the same in every project) rebuilds the `.duckdb` from `raw/` and","+  `exports/`. First thing to run on the other machine.","+- Databases with hand-curated state that the pulls cannot reproduce get one","+  `EXPORT DATABASE '<_DRIVE>/03_DATA/<project>/exports'` after each run that changes them, and the","+  other machine runs `IMPORT DATABASE` in `build_db`.","+- Sensitivity tag in each `README.md`: identifiable health data and FERPA-tagged GPS stay on Drive","+  only (Injury_Surveillance, Ath_Medicine, DEXA, the EOS GPS analysis). CFBD-derived and public","+  football data may also go to MotherDuck later if wanted.","+","+## Checklist (do on a machine with the repos on disk)","+","+Inventory first:","+","+- [ ] `find ~/DEV -name '*.duckdb' -o -name '*.db' -o -name '*.sqlite' | grep -v node_modules`","+      on the Mac; same with `Get-ChildItem -Recurse` on Windows. Record which project owns each","+      file, its size, and whether git tracks it. Likely owners from the router:","+      `DataBase_GPS_Reporting`, `ForcePlate_DecisionSystem`, `VALD_Performance`, `Catapult_API`,","+      `CFB_Victory_Model`, `CFB_Analytics_Lab`, `Risk_Stratification_Engine`, `PFF_Data_Project`.","+- [ ] For each: is it rebuildable from raw pulls, or does it carry hand-curated state? That decides","+      whether it needs an `exports/` folder.","+- [ ] For each: which machine's copy is newest? If both machines have diverged copies, do not","+      overwrite either. Export both to Parquet and diff before picking.","+","+Per project:","+","+- [ ] Add `*.duckdb`, `*.duckdb.wal`, `*.db-wal`, `*.db-shm` to `.gitignore`. If git already","+      tracks a `.duckdb`, `git rm --cached` it and note the removal in the project's `docs/STATUS.md`.","+- [ ] Point the pull script at `_DRIVE/03_DATA/<project>/raw/`. Resolve the path through the","+      `_DRIVE` link so the code is the same on both machines; do not hard-code either OS path.","+- [ ] Add `build_db` (Python or PowerShell to match the project). It reads `raw/`, imports","+      `exports/` if present, writes the local `.duckdb`.","+- [ ] Run `build_db` on the second machine and confirm the same row counts as the first.","+- [ ] Add the `README.md` with source, script, and sensitivity tag.","+","+Windows:","+","+- [ ] After the data folders are under `_DRIVE`, remove `Desktop\\DEV` from Drive for Desktop's","+      backed-up folders. This also clears the two remaining junction errors from the 09-22 handoff.","+- [ ] Confirm nothing else under `Desktop\\DEV` was relying on that Drive backup as its only copy","+      (the 09-22 note lists the three large folders; check for others over ~100 MB).","+","+Mac:","+","+- [ ] Trim the `dailybackup` manifest: drop data folders that now live under `_DRIVE`, keep the","+      CRASHBOX `ssd` tier for large regenerable outputs.","+- [ ] If pulls keep running from the Mac launchd jobs, they now write to `_DRIVE`. Confirm Drive","+      for Desktop is running when they fire, or the files sit local until it is.","+","+Router:","+","+- [ ] Add a `03_DATA` row (or wherever it lands) to `PERFORMANCE.md` and `FOOTBALL.md` in the same","+      turn the folder is created. Update `COMMANDS.md` with the `build_db` command per project.","+","+## Why not the alternatives","+","+- **Sync the `.duckdb` file itself via Drive.** Corruption risk above. Only acceptable at rest","+  (copy after the pipeline closes the file), which is what `exports/` does more safely.","+- **Commit the `.duckdb` to git.** Binary churn on every run, and the 95 MB gitignore rule already","+  excludes the big ones. Git is for the scripts, not the data.","+- **Git LFS.** Adds a paid quota and a second sync path for what Drive already does.","+- **Supabase or another Postgres.** See Decision. Wrong tool for single-user, two-machine sync.","+","+## Open questions for Eric","+","+- Which of the DuckDB files carry state that the pulls cannot rebuild? That list decides how much","+  of the `exports/` mechanism is needed at all.","+- Is `03_DATA` the right home, or should sport data go under `02_SPORTS/<sport>/data`?","+- Should the Mac stay the only machine that runs scheduled pulls, or should Windows run them too","+  now that the target is shared?"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/FOOTBALL.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PROGRAM.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RESEARCH.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/STATUS.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/handoffs/2026-09-24-data-tier-for-duckdb-and-pulls.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad9bde66-4edc-45de-833f-dfee8dc6bac7","session_id":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"02d4a48c-336d-4ffa-a0f7-cc20fd6681c5","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
