{"parentUuid":"df90559a-6146-41e3-96ad-0f1f2ee6e75f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"57b92f92-bd90-4448-a169-4e54be734ab6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# Handoff 2026-09-27: Flint day 2 (the review gate, at scale)\n\n## What and why\nDay 1 left seven sources staged, four reviews unwritten and three fix passes not applied. Day 2 ran every staged source through the two-stage review gate with parallel subagents: Sonnet fixers and atomizers, independent Opus reviewers (Codex stayed capped), and a round-2 check wherever fixes were heavy or a NO-GO was rewritten. Everything is ready for the vault; the vault write waits for Eric.\n\n## Decisions (with reasons)\n- **Work from the `step1-triage` worktree, entered by path.** The staged sources (books, OCR, audio, transcripts) are local and exist only there. Answers day 1's open question.\n- **One owner per file per wave.** Each agent got explicit write-ownership (its folder, its log, or one report). `_book.md` had a single writer at a time. File lists for the Supertraining chapter split were computed once (`staging/_scope_*.txt`) and handed to every agent, so no two agents partitioned differently.\n- **Round 2 whenever a fix pass was heavy or rewrote a NO-GO.** It paid off: Supertraining Ch1 round 2 found 12 entries still wrong; Bondarchuk round 2 found the fixer's log claimed fixes that were not in the files; Issurin round 2 found that round 1 itself had misread Issurin 2016.\n- **Reviewer citations from memory are never inserted** unless the vault or the paper confirms them. Fixers took the delete-the-clause fallback.\n- **Section headers keep the vault separator** `**What it is** —` (all 187 vault entries use it). Em dashes are banned only in titles and body text.\n- **Promotion is all-or-nothing for the S&C books** because they now cross-link (Issurin to Verkhoshansky, Bondarchuk to Supertraining, Evans to Issurin). A partial promotion would leave dangling links.\n- **No vault write without Eric.** The vault has an automated daily backup commit that could sweep a half-finished promotion.\n\n## Files created or modified (under `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\` unless noted)\n- `staging/library/**`: every staged book fixed; new entries: Supertraining 3.4.3-3.7 (36), Harries batch 2 (4), Evans (2), Bondarchuk (1). One Evans NO-GO deleted; the Bondarchuk transfer-chain entry renamed `framework--transfer-factors-general-to-competitive.md`.\n- `staging/review_*.md`: 12 new review reports (round 1 and round 2).\n- `staging/fixes_*_applied.md`: per-row fix logs. `staging/_scope_*.txt`: chapter file lists. `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-09-27.md`: every reciprocal-link suggestion, resolved to real filenames.\n- `scripts/promote_to_vault.py` (dry run and `--apply`), `scripts/lint_library.py`.\n- `docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (2026-09-27 lessons), `docs/STATUS.md`, `.gitignore` (tracks fix logs, scope lists, link list), this handoff.\n\n## Mid-flight\n- Background jobs: CFTS OCR then Zatsiorsky 2e OCR (`staging/ocr/`), CVASPS transcription (`staging/transcripts/`). They die with the session; see STATUS gotchas to restart.\n\n## Next actions\n---\n_domain_merge_sc.md\n_scope_issurin_ch3.txt\n_scope_supertraining_ch1.txt\n_scope_supertraining_ch2-3a.txt\n_scope_supertraining_ch3b.txt\nfixes_bondarchuk_ch1-2_applied.md\nfixes_evans_applied.md\nfixes_harries_batch2_applied.md\nfixes_issurin_ch1-2_applied.md\nfixes_issurin_ch3_applied.md\nfixes_oldbull_applied.md\nfixes_supertraining_ch1_round2_applied.md\nfixes_supertraining_ch2-3a_applied.md\nfixes_supertraining_ch3b_applied.md\nlibrary\nreciprocal_links_2026-09-27.md\nreview_bondarchuk_ch1-2_opus_round2.md\nreview_bondarchuk_ch1-2_opus.md\nreview_book_prompt.md\nreview_evans_opus_round2.md\nreview_evans_opus.md\nreview_harries_batch2_opus.md\nreview_harries_opus_round2.md\nreview_harries_opus.md\nreview_harries_prompt.md\nreview_issurin_ch1